  <item>
    <title>Palm Springs: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/palm-springs-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-palm-springs-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>45-day pause from Aug 26, 2026, unanimous. Council extended it on Sep 30 to the longest term California law allows, two years in total, per NBC Palm Springs. Exact end date not published in the article read.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Mendocino County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/mendocino-county-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-mendocino-county-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Supervisors voted 5-0 on Sep 1, 2026 for a 45-day urgency ordinance banning new data centers in unincorporated areas. On Oct 6, 2026 the Board voted 4-1 (Mulheren no) to extend it by 22 months 15 days to Aug 21, 2028 (original end Oct 16, 2026), narrowed so facilities under 3 MW are exempt, plus a hospital/healthcare exemption. Staff report every four months; an ad hoc committee is drafting a permanent ordinance. Sourced from news; no ordinance text read.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Humboldt County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/humboldt-county-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-humboldt-county-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Board of Supervisors voted 4-1 (Bohn dissenting) on Oct 6, 2026 for a 45-day moratorium on new data center applications in unincorporated areas, taking effect immediately per Lost Coast Outpost (45 days from Oct 6 would be Nov 20, not stated in sources). Exempts facilities under 15 MW powered 100% by on-site renewables with closed-loop water. Sources disagree on maximum extension (county agenda summary: up to 10 months 15 days). Ordinance number not found; no ordinance text read.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Lake Elsinore: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/lake-elsinore-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-lake-elsinore-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Emergency ordinance establishing a 45-day moratorium on new data center applications, unanimous, requested by Councilmember Steve Manos. Council extended it by 10 months 15 days in October 2026; the article read gives no calendar end date. City zoning code does not specifically address data centers.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Oakland: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/oakland-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-oakland-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>45-day urgency moratorium on new data centers citywide, approved 7-0, effective immediately per KTVU. Source is news (KTVU, SFist); the ordinance text was not read. No extension found as of Oct 11, 2026.</description>
