  <item>
    <title>Dixon: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/dixon-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-dixon-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>45-day interim urgency ordinance on approval of new land use applications for data centers, adopted unanimously at a special meeting Sep 30, 2026 (the city&#x27;s agenda lists the item; the vote is from press). Press says battery storage is also covered; the agenda title says data centers only. Ordinance number and effective date not found.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Arcata: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/arcata-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-arcata-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Urgency Ordinance No. 1594 (Gov Code 65858) bars the city from receiving, accepting, processing or approving data center land-use applications for 45 days from adoption; takes effect immediately. Adopted unanimously per Lost Coast Outpost (Sept 17); ordinance text read from the agenda attachment, final minutes not read. Staff expects to seek an extension (progress report due Oct 21); no extension voted as of Oct 11. Existing EdgeConneX facility unaffected.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>San Francisco: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/san-francisco-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-san-francisco-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Board of Supervisors unanimously passed a 45-day interim zoning moratorium on new and expanded data centers (Walton; File 261021 per a secondary report) on Tue Oct 6, 2026. News sources conflict on effective date (Mission Local/SFist: immediately; SF Standard: 10 days after passage unless mayor acts), so no end date is recorded; mayor signature not confirmed. Planning must study impacts; could be extended up to 22 months. No ordinance text or official Board record was read.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Hawthorne: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/hawthorne-ca</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-hawthorne-ca</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>City Council adopted interim urgency ordinance U-2270 prohibiting establishment or expansion of data centers, per PublicCEO (published Oct 2026) and a search summary; initial term 45 days with a planned extension that could bring the total to about one year. Vote tally and effective date not stated; whether the first 45 days were already extended is unknown. Council date reported as Sept 9 (a Wednesday); no ordinance text read.</description>
  </item>
